Appendix 4: 


            ARexx Status Return Values


The ARexx stratus request command is very extensive and returns a which
which can be interpruted to find out what the user is doing. The following
is a list of currently supported status return values.

0- Just startup stuff--Nothing has really happened yet..
1- Editing/Posting a mesage
2- Reading a Message
3- In CHAT with sysop
4- Adding BBS to list
5- Running standard Door
6- Running Editor Via Door
7- Viewing Bulls
8- Waitting for a call
9- Full Logon
10 Shutting down the system
11 At a menu prompt
12 Viewing Userlist
13 Searching for a user
14 Executing Dos commands
15 Doing the FIFO Door
16 Hanging up on User 
17 Running Arexx
18 Reading Personal Mail
19 Uploading
20 Downloading
21 Listing DownLoad Sections
22 Viewing file lists
23 No Logon yet, BUT connected 
24 A new User is registering
25 User is editing himself
26 Reading Internet Style Mail
27 Doing the Editors
28 Listing Message Base Boards
29 Changing MBase Area
30 Changing File Transfer Area
31 Reading a Message
32 Posting a Message
33 Scanning Messages
34 Paging the Sysop
35 Editing Macros
36 Editing Masks
37 Entering a File Description
38 Entering File Name to Download

